course: dictionary
lesson: 12520
title: Desiccate: taking the water out
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: To desiccate something is to take all the water out of it, so it becomes completely dry. Desiccated is the adjective: it describes something that has already dried out. «The desert sun desiccated the old plants» means the sun dried them out until no water was left.
explain: Use the clues around the word. «She added desiccated coconut to the cake mix.» Desiccated coconut is dry and shredded, not fresh or wet, so the meaning fits the cake. Try your meaning in the sentence: "She added dried-out coconut to the cake mix" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Desiccate is a verb, so it changes its ending: desiccate, desiccates, desiccated, desiccating. «The heat desiccated the soil last summer» tells you it happened in the past. Watch the ending, because it tells you when things happened.
fact: Desiccate is a verb: you can desiccate something, or something can be desiccated.
fact: «Desiccated» means completely dried out.
fact: Desiccated coconut is dried, shredded coconut used for baking cakes and biscuits.
fact: A desiccator is a sealed container that dries chemicals.
fact: Little packets of silica gel can keep new shoes and bags dry. They are not food: never eat them.
exercise: «The heat desiccated the puddle, and by lunchtime it was gone.» What does desiccated mean here? | *Dried out completely | Filled up with rain | Made deeper and muddier | Frozen solid
exercise: Mia says, «Use desiccated coconut in the biscuits.» What kind of coconut is it? | Sweet and sticky | Frozen in a tub | *Dried and shredded | Fresh and juicy
exercise: Which word means to take all the water out of something? | sprout | bloom | flood | *desiccate
test: «The sun desiccated the grass until it crackled like paper.» What does desiccated mean? | *Dried out completely | Cut very short | Covered with dew | Painted bright green
test: What is a desiccator used for? | Baking cakes | Growing plants | *Drying chemicals | Keeping ice cold
exam: Which sentence uses desiccated correctly? | The swimming pool was desiccated after the rain | *The river was desiccated after months with no rain | The soup was desiccated and piping hot | The puppy was desiccated and wagging its tail
